---
source: tests/cli_testing_example.rs
expression: stdout
---
A MySQL/MariaDB query tool that exports results to structured data files

Usage: gold_digger [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  completion  Generate shell completion scripts
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --db-url <URL>                   Database connection URL (mysql://user:pass@host:port/db) [env: DATABASE_URL=]
  -q, --query <SQL>                    SQL query string to execute
      --query-file <FILE>              File containing SQL query to execute
  -o, --output <FILE>                  Output file path (format inferred from extension: .csv, .json, .tsv) [env: OUTPUT_FILE=]
  -f, --format <FORMAT>                Output format override (ignores file extension) [possible values: csv, json, tsv]
  -v, --verbose...                     Enable verbose logging (-v for info, -vv for debug)
      --quiet                          Suppress all output except errors
  -p, --pretty                         Pretty-print output (only applies to JSON format)
      --allow-empty                    Exit successfully on empty result sets
      --dump-config                    Print current configuration as JSON and exit
      --tls-ca-file <TLS_CA_FILE>      Path to CA certificate file for trust anchor pinning
      --insecure-skip-hostname-verify  Skip hostname verification (keeps chain and time validation)
      --allow-invalid-certificate      Disable certificate validation entirely (DANGEROUS)
  -h, --help                           Print help
  -V, --version                        Print version
